    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "Safety\nSeguridad\nSécurité\nSicherheit\nBAe-\n146\nFederal regulations require all\npassengers to review this important\ninformation, for their safety.\nFollow these instructions, the directions\nof crew members, and placarded signs.\nWhen finished reviewing this card\nplease return it to the seat pocket for\nour next customer.\nUNITED EXPRESS.\nOperated by Air Wisconsin\nOutagamie Airport; Appleton, Wisconsin 54915-9120/(920)739-5123\n*\"UNITED EXPRESS\" is a service mark of United Airlines, Inc.\n(REV. 4/91)",
      "Bracing positions\nEmergency exits\nKnow the location and\noperation ot all exits.\nUsing the exits quickly\nevacuate the aircraft.\nBefore opening an exit,\nquickly look through a\nwindow and check outside\nfor the following:\nSmoke\nA\nB\nB\nIf smoke is so thick you\ncan not see out, redirect\npassengers to other exits.\nFire\nIf there is fire outside the\naircraft, redirect\npassengers to other exits.\nDebris\nEXIT\nIf there is metal debris or\nobstructions, redirect\npassengers to other exits.\nFollow lights to exits\nOxygen mask\nA\nMake sure the slide has inflated\ncompletely and is in good condition.\nB\nMake sure the slide has inflated\ncompletely and is in good condition.\nUse handles to stabilize slide.\nAssist others off slide.\nUse handles to stabilize slide.\nAssist others off slide.",
      "Flotation Cushion\n2\nIn water use rear exits\nonly on crew command\nCopyright © Aero Safety Graphics Inc., 1991. All Rights Reserved. Olympia, WA. USA (206) 357-9736"
    ],
